% ====================================================
% REPEAT — Isaiah 2:1–22
% Source: blue ink, photos 19, 21, 22 (PXL_20261105_235549131.jpg,
%   PXL_20261105_235610899.jpg, PXL_20261105_235616205.jpg)
% Compare with: Isaiah/2.tex (2:1–10 and 2:16 from the earlier digitization;
%   2:11–22 from the black ink, photo 20, PXL_20261105_235601350.jpg)
% ====================================================
  \pa \verse{2:1} The thing that Isaiah, son of Amoz, saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem:%
  \ed{prose}%%

  \pb \verse{2:2} It shall be in the last days\pa established\alt{set up} in the mount of the \lord's house%%

  \pb in the top of the mountains,\pa lifted up above\alt{exalted above} the hills,%%

  \pa flowing unto all the nations. \verse{2:3} Many people will go and say,%%

  \pa ``Come, we're going up into the mountain of the \lord\pa to the house of the God of Jacob.%%

  \pa He shall teach us His ways\pa and we shall walk in His paths:%%

  \pa for from Zion the law shall go forth,\pa and the word of the \lord\ from Jerusalem.''%%

  \pa \verse{2:4} He hath judged\ed{He? How? Whatever.} between the nations;\pa He hath chosen between many people.%%

  \pb They have beaten their swords into ploughshares,\pa and their spears into pruning-hooks.%%

  \pb Nation shall not lift up sword against \understood{another} nation,\pa neither do they learn\alt{are they taught} war anymore.%%

  \pa \verse{2:5} Oh house of Jacob, come\pa and we shall walk in the light of the \lord.%%

  \pa \verse{2:6} For thou hast left\alt{forsaken?} thy people,\pa the house of Jacob,%%

  \pa for they have been filled from the east\ed{note: symbolism}\pa and are sorcerers like the Philistines,\ed{Why bad here?}%%

  \pa and strike hands with the children of strangers.%%

  \pa \verse{2:7} And its land is full of silver and gold,\pa and there is no end to its treasures;%%

  \pa its land is full of horses,\pa and there is no end to its chariots.%%

  \pa \verse{2:8} Its land is full of idols;\pa it bows itself to the work of its hands:\pa that which its fingers have made.%%

  \pa \verse{2:9} The lowly man shall bow down.%%

  \pb The high is humbled\pa and you don't accept him.%%

  \pa \verse{2:10} Enter into a rock\pa and hide in the dust\alt{be hidden in dust}%%

  \pa from before\alt{the face of} the fear of the \lord\pa and from the glory of His majesty.\alt{exaltation.}%%

  \pa \verse{2:11} The lofty\alt{high} eyes of man shall be brought low\pa and the haughtiness of man shall be bowed down,%%

  \pb and the \lord\ alone shall be exalted\pa in that day.%%

  \pa \verse{2:12} For there shall be a day of the \lord\ of Hosts%%

  \pb upon all the proud and lofty\pa and upon everything that is lifted up, and it shall be brought low,\alt{humbled?}%%

  \pa \verse{2:13} and for all cedars in Lebanon:\pa the high and exalted ones,%%

  \pa and for all the oaks of Bashan,%%

  \pa \verse{2:14} and upon\alt{on} all the high mountains\pa and upon\alt{on} all the exalted heights,%
  \ed{A chiasm runs from verse~8 to verse~20, turning on ``and the \lord\ alone'' in verses~11 and~17. The Book of Mormon adds ``and upon all the nations that are lifted up'' after verse~14 and ``and upon every people'' after verse~15.}%%

  \pa \verse{2:15} and for every high tower\pa and for every fenced wall,%%

  \pa \verse{2:16} and all the ships of Tarshish%
  \ed{starting to sound like Humpty-Dumpty}
  \pa and for all beautiful ships.\alt{works of art.}%%

  \pa \verse{2:17} The haughtiness of man is bowed down\pa and the loftiness of man is humbled,%%

  \pb and the \lord\ alone shall be exalted\pa in that day.%%

  \pa \verse{2:18} And the idols\alt{heathen gods} shall be utterly destroyed.\alt{done away.}%%

  \pb \verse{2:19} And they\ie{men, idols} have entered into rock caverns~---\pa into caves\alt{tunnels} of dust%%

  \pb from the fear of the \lord\pa and the honor of His majesty\pa when He shall arise to strike\alt{terrify, shake} the earth.%%

  \pa \verse{2:20} In that day, a man shall cast away\pa all his idols of silver and gold%%

  \pa that he's made for himself to adore~---\pa to moles and bats.\ed{WTF? Cave imagery.}%%

  \pa \verse{2:21} And he shall go into rock clefts\pa and into holes in crags\alt{caves?}%%

  \pa from the fear of the \lord\pa and from His majesty's glory\pa when He shall rise to strike\alt{terrify, shake} the earth.%%

  \pa \verse{2:22} Cease ye from the man\pa who hath breath in his nostrils,%%

  \pa for why is he lightly reputed?\ed{Who cares about him?}%%

% ====================================================
% REPEAT — Isaiah 2:16
% Source: black ink, photo 20 (PXL_20261105_235601350.jpg)
% Compare with: Isaiah/2.tex 2:16 (earlier digitization)
% ====================================================
  \pa \verse{2:16} Upon all the ships of Tarshish\pa and upon all the excellent ships.%%
